style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">
                    <p>M&amp;K Field Day Team —</p>
                    <p>Thanks again to everyone who participated in our
                      Field Day 2026 debrief meeting and contributed to
                      what turned out to be a strong operation — over 50
                      years at Fort Flagler and still going strong. We
                      learned a lot this year and captured some great
                      ideas for 2027.</p>
                    <p>The <strong>After Action Review (AAR)</strong> is
                      now live and captures everything from our debrief
                      discussion: speaker contributions, improvement
                      ideas, and action items — all linked to tracked
                      issues in our planning repository.</p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> 📄
                      Field Day 2026 After Action Review </h3>
                    <p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0;"> <a
href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/blob/main/docs/debrief/aar-mk-2026-field-day-discussion.md"
style="display:inline-block;background-color:#1a3a5c;
                          color:#ffffff;padding:12px 24px;
                          text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;
                          font-weight:bold;"> View the AAR Document </a>
                    </p>
                    <p style="font-size:14px;color:#555555;"> Also
                      available: <a
                        href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/pull/29"
                        style="color:#1a3a5c;">PR #29 — Add M&amp;K Field
                        Day 2026 After Action Review</a> </p>
                    <p>The AAR covers the debrief discussion with
                      summaries of each speaker's contributions,
                      equipment issues (trailer damage, rotor failures),
                      staffing challenges, and 9+ improvement ideas
                      already converted to tracked issues.</p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> 🎯
                      Field Day 2027 Planning Project </h3>
                    <p>We've launched a <strong>public GitHub project</strong>
                      to coordinate planning for Field Day 2027. This is
                      where we're tracking all improvement ideas,
                      equipment repairs, logistics changes, and action
                      items for next year's operation.</p>
                    <table width="100%" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="0"
