                    <p>Current tracked items include trailer repairs,
                      antenna and rotor replacements, GOTA station
                      improvements, staffing coordination, and more.
                      There are already <strong>27+ improvement ideas</strong>
                      from the FD 2026 debrief.</p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> 🙋 Get
                      Involved — We Need Your Input </h3>
                    <p>You don't need to be a developer to contribute —
                      just a club member with ideas. Here's how you can
                      help make Field Day 2027 even better:</p>
                    <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Open an
                          issue</strong> — share what worked, what
                        didn't, or what you'd like to see next year.
                        Short or long, all ideas welcome. </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Comment
                          on existing issues</strong> — add your
                        thoughts, experiences, or suggestions to issues
                        already being tracked. </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Submit a
                          pull request</strong> — got documentation,
                        station notes, or procedural improvements? PRs
                        welcome! </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Browse
                          the project board</strong> — see what's
                        already being worked on and pick something to
                        help with. </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If you're not already on GitHub, it's <strong>free
                        to sign up</strong> and takes just a minute.
                      Once you have an account you can comment on issues,
                      open new ones, and help shape what we do
                      differently next year.</p>
                    <p
style="background:#fff8e1;border-left:4px solid #f0a500;
                        padding:12px 16px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;"> <strong>New
                        to GitHub?</strong> No problem. You can also <strong>reply
                        directly to this email</strong> with your
                      feedback, suggestions, or questions and I'll make
                      sure they get captured in the project. </p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> 📋
                      What We're Working On </h3>
                    <p>Some of the key areas for Field Day 2027 planning
                      include:</p>
                    <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Trailer damage
                        assessment and repairs (<a
                          href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues/25"
                          style="color:#1a3a5c;">#25</a>, <a
                          href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues/26"
                          style="color:#1a3a5c;">#26</a>)</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Antenna and rotor
                        maintenance/replacement</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">GOTA station
                        improvements and operator recruitment</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Station staffing
                        coordination and volunteer sign-ups</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Digital station
                        band planning and equipment configuration</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Radio Camp and
                        pre-event training opportunities</li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:4px;">Procedural
                        documentation and knowledge transfer</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Check the <a
                        href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues"
                        style="color:#1a3a5c;">issues list</a> for the
                      full inventory of ideas and action items.</p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> 🗓️
                      Looking Ahead </h3>
                    <p>Field Day 2027 will be held <strong>June 26–27,
                        2027</strong> (11:00 AM Saturday through 11:00
                      AM Sunday PDT), with Radio Camp starting Monday,
                      June 21. We'll be back at Fort Flagler State Park
                      continuing our 50+ year tradition.</p>
                    <p>Thanks for everything you contributed to make
                      Field Day 2026 a great event. With your continued
                      input and involvement, we'll make 2027 even
                      better!</p>
                    <p>73 de KE4HET</p>
